# The image is built from the files a release package ships
# (scripts/package-release.sh), never from whatever a working checkout has
# accumulated. A checkout that has been built holds host binaries next to
# their sources (bin/tungsten-compiler, bin/commands/build, bits/*/bin/*);
# copied into a Linux image, a macOS one of those is "newer than its source",
# so the bootstrap reuses it and dies with an exec format error.
#
# Everything is excluded, the shipped set is added back, and build products
# inside it are excluded again. Later lines win.
*

!Bitfile
!COPYRIGHT
!LICENSE-APACHE
!LICENSE-MIT
!README.md
!VERSION
!bin
!bits
!compiler
!core
!data
!doc
!implementations
!languages
!runtime
!scripts
!services

# Only the C VM bootstraps the image; the Ruby and Spinel hosts are
# maintainer options and the image carries no Ruby.
implementations/ruby
implementations/spinel

# Compiled programs have no extension; their sources and scripts do.
bin/tungsten-compiler
bin/tungsten.wc
bin/commands/*
!bin/commands/*.*
bits/*/bin/*
!bits/*/bin/*.*
bits/*/pkg

**/build
implementations/c/build*
**/tmp
**/.venv*
**/.*-cache
**/.*_cache
**/__pycache__
**/.DS_Store
**/*.dSYM
**/*.sidemap
# a built bit's manifest of the sources it was built from (bits/*/bin/<name>.deps)
bits/*/bin/*.deps
**/*.wc
**/*.ll
**/*.o
**/*.a
**/*.pyc
